style='font-size:12.0pt'>            Issues can be relatively simple in
themselves; and so the question seems about God’s reason for creating us. Issues
get complicated when we try to distinguish our own understanding from other
ones and when we have to give reasons against such alternatives, especially if
they overlap our own.&lt;span style='position:relative;top:-3.0pt'>1&lt;/span> As in
our positive presentation so also in evaluating other positions,
interpersonalism serves as the criterion for what is foreign and contradictory
to what scripture says about the nature and purpose of God and man. &lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>PRIMARY EVIDENCE FOR THE IMAGE AS THE INTERPERSONAL CAPACITY</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/nature-of-man-book/primary-evidence-for-the-image-as-the-interpersonal-capacity/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/nature-of-man-book/primary-evidence-for-the-image-as-the-interpersonal-capacity/</guid><description>&lt;style>
